          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "つもり — tsumori — \"an intention\", \"a plan\": what you mean to do. It follows a verb in its dictionary form, and です closes the sentence."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "らいねん うみに いく つもりです。 — rainen umi ni iku tsumori desu — \"I plan to go to the sea next year.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here the dictionary form matters: iku, not ikimasu, comes before つもり (tsumori). ます goes at the very end of a polite sentence, and です does that job here."
            }
          ]
        },
